DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmppssuuttiill utility can be used to display or modify various parameters
     on LSI Fusion-MPS 2 controllers.

     The mmpprruuttiill utility can be used to display or modify various parameters
     on LSI Fusion-MPS 3 controllers.

     Both the mmpprruuttiill and mmppssuuttiill commands behave identically.

     Each invocation of mmppssuuttiill consists of zero or more global options fol‐
     lowed by a command.  Commands may support additional optional or required
     arguments after the command.

     Currently one global option is supported:

     --uu _u_n_i_t
             _u_n_i_t specifies the unit of the controller to work with.  If no
             unit is specified, then unit 0 is used.

     The mmppssuuttiill utility supports several different groups of commands.  The
     first group of commands provide information about the controller.  The
     second group of commands are used to manager controller-wide operations.

     The informational commands include:

     vveerrssiioonn
             Displays the version of mmppssuuttiill.

     sshhooww aaddaapptteerr
             Displays information about the controller such as the model num‐
             ber or firmware version.

     sshhooww aaddaapptteerrss
             Displays a summary of all adapters.

     sshhooww aallll
             Displays all devices, expanders and enclosures.

     sshhooww ddeevviicceess
             Displays all devices.

     sshhooww eexxppaannddeerrss
             Displays all expanders.

     sshhooww eenncclloossuurreess
             Displays all enclosures.

     sshhooww iiooccffaaccttss
             Displays IOC Facts messages.

     sshhooww ccffggppaaggee ppaaggee [_n_u_m] [_a_d_d_r]
             Dump raw config page in hex.

     Controller management commands include:

     sseett nnccqq [_e_n_a_b_l_e|_d_i_s_a_b_l_e]
             Enables or disables NCQ in the NVRAM of the card.

     ffllaasshh ssaavvee [_f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e|_b_i_o_s] [_f_i_l_e]
             Save the _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e or _b_i_o_s from the controller into a local _f_i_l_e.
             If no _f_i_l_e is specified then the file will be named _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e or
             _b_i_o_s.

     ffllaasshh uuppddaattee [_f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e|_b_i_o_s] _f_i_l_e
             Replace the _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e or _b_i_o_s from the controller with the one
             specified via _f_i_l_e.

